  "identifier": "isbn_9781582342634",
  "title": "Booty food : a date-by-date, course-by-course, nibble-by-nibble guide to cultivating love and passion through food",
  "creator": "Malouf, Jacqui",
  "year": 2004,
  "subject": [
    "Aphrodisiac cooking",
    "Dinners and dining",
    "Food habits",
    "Cooking for two"
  ],
  "description": [
    "Includes index",
    "Phase 1: Things heat up -- 1. First date eating -- 2. In for appetizers, out for dinner -- 3. Starting slowly: the first home-cooked meal -- 4. Picnic à go-go -- 5. Is this the one? -- Phase 2: The marathon of lust -- 6. When cooking is the last thing on your mind -- 7. Foods that promote round two -- 8. Dessert's on me -- 9. Afternoon delights (nooky hooky) -- 10. Say Ahhhhhhh: get well food -- Phase 3: Now you're really cooking -- 11. Four hands are better than two -- 12. Get out of the house, for God's sake -- 13. Meet the friends already -- 14. Meet the parents: things to bring -- 15. He loves me, he loves me not -- Phase 4: Mi Cucina Es Tu Cucina -- 16. Cooking with commitment: cozy foods and flannel pajamas -- 17. Keeping It hot --18. Everything old is new again",
    "In the first guide for readers passionate about love \"and\" food, Malouf, comedian and TV food personality, combines two of life's most primal drives. \"Booty Food\" is filled with laugh-out-loud advice about dating, sex, and more than 70 delicious yet user-friendly recipes designed to complement each stage of a long-lasting love affair. Photos"
  ],
